<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48146" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thēra</span></b> , ae (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thērē</span></b> ,
		ēs), f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θήρα,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an island in the
				Ægean Sea</i>, <i>the chief of the
				Sporades</i>, now <i>Santorin</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 7,
				11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 87, 89, § 202</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">4, 12, 23, §
			70</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 6, 21,
			1</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thēraeus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Thera</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colonus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					4, 1, 139</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cyperos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 18, 70, § 117</span></i>
			.—<i>Plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thēraei</span></b> ,
				ōn, m., <i>the
				Theræans</i>, <i><span class="en">Sall. J.
				19, 3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
